  "description": "A 16 by 16 pixel drawing app with three cycling modes — solid Color, Motif + Color, and Bayer + Color — and a gallery of saved drawings.",
  "bundle": {
    "entry": "index.html",
    "files": {
      "index.html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<style>\n.tb-wrap { padding: 16px; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; }\n.tb-grid { display: block; margin: 0 auto 12px auto; border: 2px solid #111; background: #fff; cursor: pointer; touch-action: none; image-rendering: pixelated; }\n.tb-grid:focus { outline: 3px solid #111; outline-offset: 2px; }\n.tb-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.tb-row button { flex: 1; }\n\n.tb-pal, .bundle button.tb-pal { width: 48px; height: 48px; border: 2px solid #111; cursor: pointer; padding: 0; image-rendering: pixelated; }\n.tb-pal.on, .bundle button.tb-pal.on { outline: 4px solid #111; outline-offset: -4px; }\n.tb-msg { min-height: 24px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }\n.tb-gal { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 8px; }\n.tb-item { border: 2px solid #111; padding: 6px; text-align: center; }\n.tb-thumb { display: block; width: 128px; height: 128px; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n.tb-note { font-size: 13px; color: #444; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"tb-wrap\">\n<p class=\"tb-msg\" id=\"tb-msg\">Tap the canvas to paint. Tap Mode to cycle: Color, Motif + Color, Bayer + Color.</p>\n<canvas class=\"tb-grid\" id=\"tb-grid\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"3-bit art canvas\">This browser cannot draw the canvas.</canvas>\n<p class=\"tb-note\" id=\"tb-fail\" style=\"display:none\">This browser cannot draw the canvas (canvas 2D is unavailable).</p>\n<p class=\"tb-note\" id=\"tb-help\">Keyboard: focus the canvas, arrow keys move the cursor, Space paints.</p>\n<div class=\"tb-row\" id=\"tb-palette\"></div>\n<div class=\"tb-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" id=\"tb-mode\">Color</button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tb-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" id=\"tb-save\">Save to gallery</button>\n<button type=\"button\" id=\"tb-clear\">Clear</button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tb-gal\" id=\"tb-gallery\"></div>\n<p class=\"tb-note\">A kody-os rewrite of <a href=\"https://github.com/Hypercubed/3-bit-art\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hypercubed/3-bit-art</a> on GitHub.</p>\n</div>\n<script>\nvar tbScript = null;\ntry { tbScript = document.currentScript; } catch (err) { tbScript = null; }\nvar tbSection = null;\n(function () {\n  var el = tbScript;\n  while (el) {\n    if (el.getAttribute && el.getAttribute('data-app-id')) { tbSection = el; break; }\n    el = el.parentNode;\n  }\n  if (!tbSection) {\n    var secs = document.querySelectorAll('section[data-app-id]');\n    if (secs.length > 0) { tbSection = secs[0]; }\n  }\n})();\n// Three display modes, cycled by one Mode button, in this order:\n// Color (solid 3-bit RGB cube), Motif + Color (the 16x16 motif blocks\n// below, with the majority area in the original colour and the motif\n// in black or white), and Bayer + Color (a 32x32 Bayer ordered-dither\n// block, with the majority pixels in the original colour and the\n// minority pixels in black or white). On a colour screen the colour\n// shows; on the Kindle the colour collapses to luma grey, so the\n// Kindle view of Motif + Color is motif plus luma grey, and the\n// Kindle view of Bayer + Color is Bayer plus luma grey.\n// The motif blocks: eight 16x16 blocks, one per value. Each block\n// repeats an 8x8 tile 2x2, so the feature count is the spec count:\n// green gets 4 horizontal lines, cyan 4 vertical lines, yellow and\n// blue get 16 dots. Motif separates the close luma pairs: black solid\n// vs blue sparse white dots, red down-right vs magenta down-left\n// diagonals, green horizontal vs cyan vertical lines, yellow sparse\n// dots vs white solid. Every tile is period 4 except the two solids,\n// so the 2x2 repeat is seamless. Yellow and blue dots are shifted\n// by 2 pattern pixels right and down (dots at 2, 6, 10, 14, not 0, 4,\n// 8, 12), green lines down 2 and cyan lines right 2, for centre\n// symmetry; the period is still 4, so spacing across cell\n// boundaries stays 4.\n// Crispness rule: a pattern pixel must map to an integer number of\n// device pixels, at every stage, with no fractional scaling anywhere.\n// So the board cell size in device pixels is always a multiple of\n// 32 (the least common multiple of the 16-pixel motif block and the\n// 32-pixel Bayer block), the tile fills the whole cell with no gap\n// inset, and palette buttons are canvases built directly at a\n// multiple-of-32 device size, not a scaled vector or bitmap. Cells\n// abut edge to edge: no gap, no grey background showing between\n// cells. Gallery thumbnails stay solid colour in all three modes:\n// at 8 device pixels per thumbnail cell a 16- or 32-pixel block\n// would need pattern pixels smaller than one device pixel, which\n// cannot be crisp.\n// Mode migration: the old 'pattern' mode (motif in black and white)\n// no longer exists; saved state with mode 'pattern' is read as\n// 'motif-color', the closest successor, and saved state with an\n// unknown mode falls back to 'color', the first mode in the cycle.\nvar TB_TILE = 16;\nvar TB_LUM = [0, 54, 182, 237, 18, 73, 201, 255];\nvar TB_PATTERN_ROWS = [\n  [\"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\"],\n  [\"11101110\", \"01110111\", \"10111011\", \"11011101\", \"11101110\", \"01110111\", \"10111011\", \"11011101\"],\n  [\"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"11111111\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"11111111\", \"00000000\"],\n  [\"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00100010\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00100010\", \"00000000\"],\n  [\"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11011101\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11111111\", \"11011101\", \"11111111\"],\n  [\"11101110\", \"11011101\", \"10111011\", \"01110111\", \"11101110\", \"11011101\", \"10111011\", \"01110111\"],\n  [\"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\", \"00100010\"],\n  [\"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\", \"00000000\"]\n];\nfunction tbPattern(v) {\n  var rows = TB_PATTERN_ROWS[v], m = [], r, c;\n  for (r = 0; r < 16; r++) {\n    m[r] = [];\n    for (c = 0; c < 16; c++) {\n      m[r][c] = rows[r % 8].charAt(c % 8) === '1' ? 1 : 0;\n    }\n  }\n  return m;\n}\nvar TB_PATTERNS = (function () {\n  var out = [], v;\n  for (v = 0; v < 8; v++) { out.push(tbPattern(v)); }\n  return out;\n})();\nvar TB_MODES = ['color', 'motif-color', 'bayer-color'];\nvar TB_MODE_LABELS = { 'color': 'Color', 'motif-color': 'Motif + Color', 'bayer-color': 'Bayer + Color' };\nfunction tbNormalizeMode(m) {\n  if (m === 'pattern') { return 'motif-color'; }\n  if (TB_MODES.indexOf(m) >= 0) { return m; }\n  return 'color';\n}\nfunction tbBayerMatrix(n) {\n  if (n === 1) { return [[0]]; }\n  var m = tbBayerMatrix(n / 2), out = [], h2 = n / 2, y, x, v;\n  for (y = 0; y < n; y++) { out[y] = []; }\n  for (y = 0; y < h2; y++) {\n    for (x = 0; x < h2; x++) {\n      v = m[y][x];\n      out[y][x] = 4 * v;\n      out[y][x + h2] = 4 * v + 2;\n      out[y + h2][x] = 4 * v + 3;\n      out[y + h2][x + h2] = 4 * v + 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nvar TB_BAYER = tbBayerMatrix(32);\nfunction tbBayerPattern(v) {\n  var lum = TB_LUM[v] || 0, m = [], r, c;\n  for (r = 0; r < 32; r++) {\n    m[r] = [];\n    for (c = 0; c < 32; c++) {\n      m[r][c] = (TB_BAYER[r][c] / 1024 < (1 - lum / 255)) ? 1 : 0;\n    }\n  }\n  return m;\n}\nvar TB_BAYER_PATTERNS = (function () {\n  var out = [], v;\n  for (v = 0; v < 8; v++) { out.push(tbBayerPattern(v)); }\n  return out;\n})();\nfunction tbMotifMajorityBlack(v) {\n  var total = 0, r, c;\n  for (r = 0; r < 16; r++) {\n    for (c = 0; c < 16; c++) { total += TB_PATTERNS[v][r][c]; }\n  }\n  return total >= 128;\n}\nfunction tbMotifPixelColor(v, bit) {\n  if (tbMotifMajorityBlack(v)) { return bit === 1 ? TB_COLORS[v] : '#ffffff'; }\n  return bit === 1 ? '#000000' : TB_COLORS[v];\n}\nfunction tbBayerPixelColor(v, isBlack) {\n  if ((TB_LUM[v] || 0) < 128) { return isBlack ? TB_COLORS[v] : '#ffffff'; }\n  return isBlack ? '#000000' : TB_COLORS[v];\n}\nfunction tbGrey(v) {\n  var g = TB_LUM[v] || 0;\n  return 'rgb(' + g + ',' + g + ',' + g + ')';\n}\nvar tbStore = null;\nvar tbState = { data: '', gallery: '', mode: 'color' };\n// Color mode uses the standard 3-bit RGB cube, same bit order as the luma\n// mapping (R = bit 0, G = bit 1, B = bit 2). Mode is saved in state, so a\n// color display stays in color and the Scribe stays in pattern, with no\n// device detection: colorDepth reports 24-bit and the monochrome media\n// query is false on the Scribe, so neither can tell the two apart.\nvar TB_COLORS = ['#000000', '#ff0000', '#00ff00', '#ffff00', '#0000ff', '#ff00ff', '#00ffff', '#ffffff'];\nvar tbColor = 1;\nvar tbDragging = false;\nvar tbLastGallery = '';\nvar tbLastMode = '';\nvar tbCanvas = null;\nvar tbCtx = null;\nvar tbCellCss = 32;\nvar tbCellDev = 32;\nvar tbGapDev = 0;\nvar tbDpr = 1;\nvar tbCursor = 8 * 16 + 8;\nvar tbFocused = false;\nvar tbLastPaintIdx = -1;\nvar tbLastPaintAt = 0;\nvar tbLastDrawnData = '';\nvar tbLastDrawnMode = '';\nvar tbTileCanvases = [];\nvar tbTileMode = '';\nvar tbPalCanvases = [];\nvar tbPalDev = 48;\nvar tbPalCss = 48;\nfunction tbEmptyData() {\n  var s = '', i;\n  for (i = 0; i < 256; i++) { s += '7'; }\n  return s;\n}\nfunction tbPalSize(dpr) {\n  var s = Math.round(48 * dpr / 32) * 32;\n  if (s < 32) { s = 32; }\n  return s;\n}\nfunction tbLayout() {\n  var canvas = document.getElementById('tb-grid');\n  if (!canvas) { return false; }\n  var wrap = canvas.parentNode;\n  var avail = wrap && wrap.clientWidth ? wrap.clientWidth : 560;\n  var style = wrap && window.getComputedStyle ? window.getComputedStyle(wrap) : null;\n  var padL = style ? (parseInt(style.paddingLeft, 10) || 0) : 16;\n  var padR = style ? (parseInt(style.paddingRight, 10) || 0) : 16;\n  avail = avail - padL - padR;\n  if (avail < 16 * 8) { avail = 528; }\n  var dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (dpr < 1) { dpr = 1; }\n  if (dpr > 2) { dpr = 2; }\n  // Crispness: cell size in device pixels must be a multiple of 32,\n  // so one motif pattern pixel is exactly cellDev/16 device pixels\n  // and one Bayer pattern pixel is exactly cellDev/32 device pixels,\n  // uniform for every pattern pixel. Round the available per-cell\n  // device size to the nearest multiple of 32\n  // (32 at the usual ~30 device pixels per cell, 64 at ratio 2),\n  // then derive the CSS size from the device size, never the other\n  // way round, so backing store equals CSS size times dpr exactly.\n  var perCellDev = avail * dpr / 16;\n  var cellDev = Math.round(perCellDev / 32) * 32;\n  if (cellDev < 32) { cellDev = 32; }\n  tbCellCss = cellDev / dpr;\n  tbCellDev = cellDev;\n  tbDpr = dpr;\n  tbGapDev = 0;\n  tbPalDev = tbPalSize(dpr);\n  tbPalCss = tbPalDev / dpr;\n  var devW = cellDev * 16;\n  var devH = cellDev * 16;\n  if (canvas.width !== devW || canvas.height !== devH) {\n    canvas.width = devW;\n    canvas.height = devH;\n  }\n  canvas.style.width = (cellDev * 16 / dpr) + 'px';\n  canvas.style.height = (cellDev * 16 / dpr) + 'px';\n  if ('imageSmoothingEnabled' in tbCtx) { tbCtx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; }\n  if ('webkitImageSmoothingEnabled' in tbCtx) { tbCtx.webkitImageSmoothingEnabled = false; }\n  tbBuildTiles();\n  return true;\n}\nfunction tbBuildTileCanvas(v, size) {\n  var tile = document.createElement('canvas');\n  tile.width = size;\n  tile.height = size;\n  var g = null;\n  try { g = tile.getContext('2d'); } catch (err) { g = null; }\n  if (!g) { return null; }\n  var px, py, n, pp;\n  if (tbState.mode === 'color') {\n    g.fillStyle = TB_COLORS[v] || '#ffffff';\n    g.fillRect(0, 0, size, size);\n    return tile;\n  }\n  if (tbState.mode === 'bayer-color') {\n    n = 32;\n    pp = size / 32;\n    for (py = 0; py < 32; py++) {\n      for (px = 0; px < 32; px++) {\n        g.fillStyle = tbBayerPixelColor(v, TB_BAYER_PATTERNS[v][py][px] === 1);\n        g.fillRect(px * pp, py * pp, pp, pp);\n      }\n    }\n    return tile;\n  }\n  pp = size / 16;\n  for (py = 0; py < 16; py++) {\n    for (px = 0; px < 16; px++) {\n      g.fillStyle = tbMotifPixelColor(v, TB_PATTERNS[v][py][px]);\n      g.fillRect(px * pp, py * pp, pp, pp);\n    }\n  }\n  return tile;\n}\nfunction tbBuildTiles() {\n  var size = tbCellDev;\n  var v;\n  tbTileMode = tbState.mode;\n  tbTileCanvases = [];\n  tbPalCanvases = [];\n  for (v = 0; v < 8; v++) {\n    tbTileCanvases[v] = tbBuildTileCanvas(v, size);\n    tbPalCanvases[v] = tbBuildTileCanvas(v, tbPalDev);\n  }\n}\nfunction tbDrawCell(idx) {\n  if (!tbCtx) { return; }\n  var x = idx % 16;\n  var y = Math.floor(idx / 16);\n  var v = parseInt(tbState.data.charAt(idx), 10) || 0;\n  if (v < 0 || v > 7) { v = 0; }\n  var gx = x * tbCellDev;\n  var gy = y * tbCellDev;\n  var size = tbCellDev;\n  if (tbState.mode === 'color') {\n    tbCtx.fillStyle = TB_COLORS[v] || '#ffffff';\n    tbCtx.fillRect(gx, gy, size, size);\n    return;\n  }\n  var tile = tbTileCanvases[v];\n  if (tile) {\n    try { tbCtx.drawImage(tile, gx, gy); } catch (err) { tbCtx.fillStyle = '#fff'; tbCtx.fillRect(gx, gy, size, size); }\n  } else {\n    tbCtx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n    tbCtx.fillRect(gx, gy, size, size);\n  }\n}\nfunction tbDrawAll() {\n  if (!tbCtx) { return; }\n  tbCtx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n  tbCtx.fillRect(0, 0, tbCanvas.width, tbCanvas.height);\n  for (var i = 0; i < 256; i++) { tbDrawCell(i); }\n  if (tbFocused) {\n    var cx = (tbCursor % 16) * tbCellDev;\n    var cy = Math.floor(tbCursor / 16) * tbCellDev;\n    var t = Math.max(2, Math.round(tbDpr * 2));\n    tbCtx.fillStyle = '#111';\n    tbCtx.fillRect(cx, cy, tbCellDev, t);\n    tbCtx.fillRect(cx, cy + tbCellDev - t, tbCellDev, t);\n    tbCtx.fillRect(cx, cy, t, tbCellDev);\n    tbCtx.fillRect(cx + tbCellDev - t, cy, t, tbCellDev);\n  }\n}\nfunction tbCellAt(e) {\n  if (!tbCanvas) { return -1; }\n  var rect = tbCanvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  var borderL = tbCanvas.clientLeft || 0;\n  var borderT = tbCanvas.clientTop || 0;\n  var width = tbCanvas.clientWidth || rect.width || (tbCellCss * 16);\n  var height = tbCanvas.clientHeight || rect.height || (tbCellCss * 16);\n  var x = Math.floor((e.clientX - rect.left - borderL) / (width / 16));\n  var y = Math.floor((e.clientY - rect.top - borderT) / (height / 16));\n  if (x < 0 || x >= 16 || y < 0 || y >= 16) { return -1; }\n  return y * 16 + x;\n}\nfunction tbPaintAt(e) {\n  var idx = tbCellAt(e);\n  if (idx < 0) { return; }\n  tbCursor = idx;\n  tbPaint(idx);\n  if (tbFocused) { tbDrawAll(); }\n}\nfunction tbTouchPoint(e) {\n  if (e.touches && e.touches.length > 0) { return e.touches[0]; }\n  if (e.changedTouches && e.changedTouches.length > 0) { return e.changedTouches[0]; }\n  return null;\n}\nfunction tbKeyName(e) {\n  if (e.key) { return e.key; }\n  var c = e.keyCode;\n  if (c === 37) { return 'ArrowLeft'; }\n  if (c === 38) { return 'ArrowUp'; }\n  if (c === 39) { return 'ArrowRight'; }\n  if (c === 40) { return 'ArrowDown'; }\n  if (c === 32) { return ' '; }\n  if (c === 13) { return 'Enter'; }\n  return '';\n}\nfunction tbWireBoard() {\n  var c = tbCanvas;\n  if (!c) { return; }\n  c.addEventListener('mousedown', function (e) {\n    if (e.button && e.button !== 0) { return; }\n    tbDragging = true;\n    tbLastPaintIdx = -1;\n    tbPaintAt(e);\n    e.preventDefault();\n  });\n  c.addEventListener('mousemove', function (e) {\n    if (!tbDragging) { return; }\n    if (e.buttons !== undefined && (e.buttons & 1) !== 1) { return; }\n    tbPaintAt(e);\n  });\n  c.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { tbDragging = false; });\n  document.addEventListener('mouseup', function () { tbDragging = false; });\n  c.addEventListener('touchstart', function (e) {\n    var t = tbTouchPoint(e);\n    if (!t) { return; }\n    tbDragging = true;\n    tbLastPaintIdx = -1;\n    tbPaintAt(t);\n    e.preventDefault();\n  }, false);\n  c.addEventListener('touchmove', function (e) {\n    if (!tbDragging) { return; }\n    var t = tbTouchPoint(e);\n    if (!t) { return; }\n    tbPaintAt(t);\n    e.preventDefault();\n  }, false);\n  c.addEventListener('touchend', function () { tbDragging = false; }, false);\n  c.addEventListener('touchcancel', function () { tbDragging = false; }, false);\n  c.addEventListener('focus', function () { tbFocused = true; tbDrawAll(); });\n  c.addEventListener('blur', function () { tbFocused = false; tbDrawAll(); });\n  c.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {\n    var key = tbKeyName(e);\n    var x = tbCursor % 16;\n    var y = Math.floor(tbCursor / 16);\n    if (key === ' ' || key === 'Spacebar' || key === 'Enter') {\n      tbPaint(tbCursor);\n      if (tbFocused) { tbDrawAll(); }\n      e.preventDefault();\n      return;\n    }\n    if (key === 'ArrowLeft' || key === 'Left') { x -= 1; }\n    else if (key === 'ArrowRight' || key === 'Right') { x += 1; }\n    else if (key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'Up') { y -= 1; }\n    else if (key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 'Down') { y += 1; }\n    else { return; }\n    e.preventDefault();\n    if (x < 0) { x = 0; }\n    if (x >= 16) { x = 15; }\n    if (y < 0) { y = 0; }\n    if (y >= 16) { y = 15; }\n    tbCursor = y * 16 + x;\n    tbDrawAll();\n  });\n}\nfunction tbRebase(server, pending, sent) { return { args: pending, optimistic: pending }; }\nfunction tbSave(next) {\n  tbState = { data: next.data, gallery: next.gallery, mode: tbNormalizeMode(next.mode || tbState.mode) };\n  tbRender();\n  if (tbStore) { tbStore.dispatch('save', tbState, tbState, tbRebase); }\n}\nfunction tbSetMsg(text) {\n  var el = document.getElementById('tb-msg');\n  if (el) { el.textContent = text; }\n}\nfunction tbPaint(idx) {\n  var now = Date.now ? Date.now() : new Date().getTime();\n  if (idx === tbLastPaintIdx && now - tbLastPaintAt < 120) { return; }\n  tbLastPaintIdx = idx;\n  tbLastPaintAt = now;\n  var cells = tbState.data.split('');\n  cells[idx] = String(tbColor);\n  var next = cells.join('');\n  if (next === tbState.data) { return; }\n  tbState.data = next;\n  tbLastDrawnData = next;\n  if (tbCanvas && tbCtx) { tbDrawCell(idx); }\n  if (tbStore) { tbStore.dispatch('save', tbState, tbState, tbRebase); }\n}\nfunction tbRenderGrid() {\n  if (!tbCtx) { return; }\n  if (tbState.data === tbLastDrawnData && tbState.mode === tbLastDrawnMode) { return; }\n  tbDrawAll();\n  tbLastDrawnData = tbState.data;\n  tbLastDrawnMode = tbState.mode;\n}\nfunction tbRenderGallery() {\n  var gal = document.getElementById('tb-gallery');\n  if (!gal) { return; }\n  while (gal.firstChild) { gal.removeChild(gal.firstChild); }\n  if (!tbState.gallery) { return; }\n  var items = tbState.gallery.split('|');\n  for (var k = 0; k < items.length; k++) {\n    (function (idx, drawing) {\n      var item = document.createElement('div');\n      item.className = 'tb-item';\n      var thumb = document.createElement('canvas');\n      thumb.className = 'tb-thumb';\n      var dpr = Math.round(tbDpr);\n      if (dpr < 1) { dpr = 1; }\n      if (dpr > 2) { dpr = 2; }\n      thumb.width = 128 * dpr;\n      thumb.height = 128 * dpr;\n      thumb.style.width = '128px';\n      thumb.style.height = '128px';\n      var g = null;\n      try { g = thumb.getContext('2d'); } catch (err) { g = null; }\n      if (g) {\n        var px = thumb.width / 16;\n        var p, v;\n        for (p = 0; p < 256 && p < drawing.length; p++) {\n          v = parseInt(drawing.charAt(p), 10) || 0;\n          if (v < 0 || v > 7) { v = 0; }\n          g.fillStyle = TB_COLORS[v] || '#ffffff';\n          g.fillRect((p % 16) * px, Math.floor(p / 16) * px, px, px);\n        }\n      }\n      var load = document.createElement('button');\n      load.type = 'button';\n      load.textContent = 'Load';\n      load.addEventListener('click', function () {\n        tbSetMsg('Loaded drawing ' + (idx + 1) + ' from the gallery.');\n        tbSave({ data: drawing, gallery: tbState.gallery });\n      });\n      var del = document.createElement('button');\n      del.type = 'button';\n      del.textContent = 'Delete';\n      del.addEventListener('click', function () {\n        var rest = tbState.gallery.split('|');\n        rest.splice(idx, 1);\n        tbSetMsg('Deleted drawing ' + (idx + 1) + '.');\n        tbSave({ data: tbState.data, gallery: rest.join('|') });\n      });\n      item.appendChild(thumb);\n      item.appendChild(load);\n      item.appendChild(del);\n      gal.appendChild(item);\n    })(k, items[k]);\n  }\n}\nfunction tbRender() {\n  // Rebuild tiles BEFORE drawing the grid: the grid cache records\n  // the mode it drew, so drawing first with old tiles and rebuilding\n  // after would leave the board one mode behind the button and the\n  // palette, which only redraw on the next render.\n  if (tbTileMode !== tbState.mode) { tbBuildTiles(); }\n  if (tbState.data && tbState.data.length === 256) {\n    tbRenderGrid();\n  }\n  if (tbState.gallery !== tbLastGallery || tbState.mode !== tbLastMode) {\n    tbLastGallery = tbState.gallery;\n    tbLastMode = tbState.mode;\n    tbRenderGallery();\n  }\n  var pals = document.querySelectorAll('.tb-pal');\n  for (var i = 0; i < pals.length; i++) {\n    var pv = parseInt(pals[i].getAttribute('data-color'), 10) || 0;\n    if (pv === tbColor) { pals[i].className = 'tb-pal on'; }\n    else { pals[i].className = 'tb-pal'; }\n    if (pals[i].tagName === 'CANVAS') {\n      if (pals[i].width !== tbPalDev || pals[i].height !== tbPalDev) {\n        pals[i].width = tbPalDev;\n        pals[i].height = tbPalDev;\n        pals[i].style.width = tbPalCss + 'px';\n        pals[i].style.height = tbPalCss + 'px';\n      }\n      var pg = null;\n      try { pg = pals[i].getContext('2d'); } catch (err) { pg = null; }\n      if (pg) {\n        if ('imageSmoothingEnabled' in pg) { pg.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; }\n        var ptile = tbPalCanvases[pv];\n        if (ptile) { try { pg.drawImage(ptile, 0, 0); } catch (err) { pg.fillStyle = '#fff'; pg.fillRect(0, 0, tbPalDev, tbPalDev); } }\n        else { pg.fillStyle = '#fff'; pg.fillRect(0, 0, tbPalDev, tbPalDev); }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  var modeBtn = document.getElementById('tb-mode');\n  if (modeBtn) { modeBtn.textContent = TB_MODE_LABELS[tbNormalizeMode(tbState.mode)] || 'Color'; }\n}\nfunction tbInit() {\n  if (window.KodyBridge && tbSection) {\n    tbStore = window.KodyBridge.create(tbSection, {\n      fieldTypes: { data: 'string', gallery: 'string' },\n      reassert: function (desired) { return { action: 'save', args: desired, optimistic: desired, rebase: tbRebase }; }\n    });\n    tbStore.subscribe(function (snap) {\n      var d = snap.desired;\n      if (d && typeof d.data === 'string' && d.data.length === 256) {\n        tbState = { data: d.data, gallery: d.gallery || '', mode: tbNormalizeMode(d.mode) };\n        tbRender();\n      }\n    });\n    tbStore.startSpanObserver();\n    var cur = tbStore.getState().desired;\n    if (cur && typeof cur.data === 'string' && cur.data.length === 256) {\n      tbState = { data: cur.data, gallery: cur.gallery || '', mode: tbNormalizeMode(cur.mode) };\n    }\n  } else {\n    var seed = null;\n    var scripts = document.querySelectorAll('script[data-kody-state-seed]');\n    for (var s = 0; s < scripts.length; s++) {\n      try { seed = JSON.parse(scripts[s].textContent); } catch (err) { seed = null; }\n      if (seed) { break; }\n    }\n    if (seed && typeof seed.data === 'string' && seed.data.length === 256) {\n      tbState = { data: seed.data, gallery: seed.gallery || '', mode: tbNormalizeMode(seed.mode) };\n    } else {\n      tbState = { data: tbEmptyData(), gallery: '', mode: 'color' };\n    }\n  }\n  if (!tbState.data || tbState.data.length !== 256) { tbState.data = tbEmptyData(); }\n  tbState.mode = tbNormalizeMode(tbState.mode);\n  var canvas = document.getElementById('tb-grid');\n  if (canvas && canvas.getContext) {\n    try { tbCtx = canvas.getContext('2d'); } catch (err) { tbCtx = null; }\n  }\n  if (canvas && tbCtx) {\n    tbCanvas = canvas;\n    tbCursor = 8 * 16 + 8;\n    tbLayout();\n    tbWireBoard();\n  } else {\n    if (canvas) { canvas.style.display = 'none'; }\n    var fail = document.getElementById('tb-fail');\n    if (fail) { fail.style.display = ''; }\n  }\n  var pal = document.getElementById('tb-palette');\n  if (pal) {\n    for (var c = 0; c < 8; c++) {\n      (function (idx) {\n        var b = document.createElement('canvas');\n        b.className = idx === tbColor ? 'tb-pal on' : 'tb-pal';\n        b.width = tbPalDev;\n        b.height = tbPalDev;\n        b.style.width = tbPalCss + 'px';\n        b.style.height = tbPalCss + 'px';\n        b.setAttribute('role', 'button');\n        b.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');\n        b.setAttribute('data-color', String(idx));\n        b.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Pattern ' + idx);\n        b.addEventListener('click', function () { tbColor = idx; tbRender(); });\n        pal.appendChild(b);\n      })(c);\n    }\n  }\n  window.addEventListener('resize', function () {\n    if (tbCanvas && tbLayout()) {\n      tbDrawAll();\n      tbLastDrawnData = tbState.data;\n      tbLastDrawnMode = tbState.mode;\n    }\n  });\n  var modeBtn = document.getElementById('tb-mode');\n  if (modeBtn) {\n    modeBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      var cur = tbNormalizeMode(tbState.mode);\n      var idx = TB_MODES.indexOf(cur);\n      var nm = TB_MODES[(idx + 1) % TB_MODES.length];\n      tbLastGallery = '';\n      tbSave({ data: tbState.data, gallery: tbState.gallery, mode: nm });\n    });\n  }\n  var save = document.getElementById('tb-save');\n  if (save) {\n    save.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      var items = tbState.gallery ? tbState.gallery.split('|') : [];\n      if (items.length >= 12) {\n        tbSetMsg('Gallery is full (12). Delete one first.');\n        return;\n      }\n      items.push(tbState.data);\n      tbSetMsg('Saved to gallery (' + items.length + ' of 12).');\n      tbSave({ data: tbState.data, gallery: items.join('|') });\n    });\n  }\n  var clr = document.getElementById('tb-clear');\n  if (clr) {\n    clr.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      tbSetMsg('Canvas cleared.');\n      tbSave({ data: tbEmptyData(), gallery: tbState.gallery });\n    });\n  }\n  tbRender();\n}\nif (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', tbInit);\n} else {\n  tbInit();\n}\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
